  <title id="noisedensity-title">Voltage noise density of an amplifier with a 1/f corner at 10 hertz</title>
  <desc id="noisedensity-desc">On logarithmic axes, the noise density is flat at 10 nanovolts per root hertz above about 10 hertz and rises with falling frequency below it, as one over the square root of frequency, reaching about 316 nanovolts per root hertz at 0.01 hertz. The corner frequency, where the two asymptotes meet, is 10 hertz; there the density is the square root of two times the white level.</desc>
